# Cerebro core rules

## Stack and commands
- React + TypeScript + Vite, three.js with troika text, GSAP (core only, no plugins), Express dev server in `server.ts`.
- Typecheck: `npm run lint` (`tsc --noEmit`). Tests: `npm test` (self-tests), `npm run test:voice`. Build: `npm run build`.
- Run typecheck and tests before committing. Fix failures your change causes.

## Code style
- Imports at the top of the module. No inline or dynamic imports unless a circular dependency forces it, and then document why.
- Switches over unions or enums end with a `never` check in `default`.
- Comments explain non-obvious intent only. Never narrate what the code does.
- Do not edit `src/three_LOCKED_BASELINE/`. It is a frozen reference.
- `.agents/` and `.aistudio/` are untracked tooling folders. Do not commit them.

## Honest state (non-negotiable)
- Never invent metrics, percentages, playback, or media. Unreviewed media keeps `runtimeUrl: null` and renders a placeholder card with a `blocked` or `pending-media` status.
- Node status vocabulary: verified, proposed, gap, disconnected, unverified. Use it as is.
- Status UI (`system-status-layer`, `verified-progress`) reads real data or shows nothing.

## Registry and naming
- Nodes, anchors and environments come from `src/data/environmentRegistry.ts`. Do not hard-code node positions elsewhere.
- Registry ids match `^[a-z]+__[a-z]+__[a-z0-9]+(_[a-z0-9]+)*$`.
- Khalid is always `khalid` / "Khalid Alshaalan".
- Add `data-testid` to every new interactive element. Keep existing test ids stable.

## Git
- Work on the current branch unless told otherwise. Commit in small logical steps with descriptive messages. Do not open a PR unless asked.
- Never write tokens or secrets into files, commits, or messages.
